  "publisher": "SPiER Project",
  "description": "FHIR Questionnaire for the full Patient Safety Screener / Suicide Risk Screener — a combined acute-care instrument that pairs the ED-SAFE universal screen (the three PSS-3 items: depression, active ideation, lifetime attempt + recency) with a site-defined risk-stratification step. It is used at the Clarify Risk stage in EDs/inpatient settings that want a single combined screen-and-stratify tool. The universal screen wording is the ED-SAFE PSS-3; the risk-stratification tier is determined per the site's local protocol and clinician judgment (SPiER does not embed a proprietary secondary instrument).",
  "purpose": "Screen and stratify suicide risk in one acute-care encounter. The three screening items follow the public PSS-3; the risk-level result is a site-defined stratification bound to the common SPiER suicide-risk tier, so the derived Observation lands directly on the concept layer (no per-instrument crosswalk).",
  "copyright": "The PSS-3 screening items were developed at the University of Massachusetts Medical School through the ED-SAFE studies, funded by the National Institute of Mental Health, and are available for download from the Suicide Prevention Resource Center. Their published materials state no copyright notice and no permission terms; confirm the terms of reuse with the developers before deployment. The risk-stratification step is site-defined. Used under the license/permission held by the SPiER project.",
